From e41058fc7e9c0440c7446b825cd0bc234a1d8ba8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 09:27:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/51] =?UTF-8?q?begonia=20(MT6785):=20conn/WiFi=20bring-u?=
 =?UTF-8?q?p=20WIP=20=E2=80=94=20conninfra=20+=20btif=20+=20mt7615=20AXI?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20graft=20+=20DT?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Out-of-tree integration of the begonia connectivity/WiFi bring-up onto
mt6785-mainline 6.16.4:
- drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-conninfra-mt6785.c  (conn_infra bring-up to COM=0x1d1e)
- drivers/misc/mtk-btif.c (+hdr)               (BTIF transport to the conn-MCU)
- drivers/net/wireless/.../mt7615/soc_mt6785.c (connac1.0 AXI graft, is_mt6785 token)
- arch/arm64/.../mt6785-xiaomi-begonia.dts + mt6785.dtsi (consys/btif/wmac + EMI carveout)

State: conn-MCU reaches idle + autonomously arms its RX-DMA (ch7, =stock);
open gate = conn firmware never advances from ROM-idle into its servicing loop.

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
